# Documentation Management Rules

## Purpose
Define how the agent creates and updates documentation under `<DOCS_ROOT>` (`<PROJECT_DIR>/docs` by default, or `$GDMETAPRO_DOCS_ROOT`).

## When To Apply
Apply when the user asks to create or update documentation, plans, requirements, communication notes, reports, or review artifacts.

## Requirements Packages
Anything under `docs/requirements/<name>/` (README, PRD, specification, and
their optional companions, including `implementation-plan.md`) follows
`requirements-package-standard.mdc`. Do not restate or diverge from that
layout here: no date-stamped subfolders, no mandatory `ru`/`en`/`ai` variants —
the `Version: x.y.z` field on each document is the versioning mechanism.

## Mandatory Behavior
1. Ask for target location and folder name before writing any doc.
2. Do not date-stamp folders. Write into `<category>/<name>/` and update
   documents in place, bumping their `Version` field where the category's
   standard defines one (requirements packages always do).
3. Default to `en` output. Add other language variants only when the user
   explicitly asks for them, and keep any variants you do create synchronized.
4. Update `<DOCS_ROOT>/README.md` after doc changes.
5. Ask whether to apply changes (branch/commit/PR) after edits.

## Required Locations
- Root: `<DOCS_ROOT>` (default: `<PROJECT_DIR>/docs`)
- Standard pattern: `<DOCS_ROOT>/<category>/<name>/`
- Requirements packages: `<DOCS_ROOT>/requirements/<name>/` per
  `requirements-package-standard.mdc` (no date folder).

## DOCS_ROOT Resolution

The docs root is resolved in this priority order:

1. **`DOCS_ROOT` passed explicitly** by the orchestrator in the sub-agent dispatch prompt
2. **`GDMETAPRO_DOCS_ROOT` environment variable** (if set in the shell)
3. **`<PROJECT_DIR>/docs/`** — default, relative to the project being worked on

```bash
DOCS_ROOT="${GDMETAPRO_DOCS_ROOT:-$PROJECT_DIR/docs}"
```

`PROJECT_DIR` is always known by Phase 0.2 of the orchestrator. Sub-agents (context-collector, feature-analyzer, etc.) **never resolve DOCS_ROOT themselves** — they receive it explicitly from the orchestrator.

## Category Definitions

| Category | Path pattern | Description |
|----------|-------------|-------------|
| `requirements` | `docs/requirements/<name>/` | See `requirements-package-standard.mdc`. |
| `plans` | `docs/plans/<name>/` | Standalone implementation plans not tied to a requirements package. A plan that belongs to one lives inside that package as `implementation-plan.md` instead — see `requirements-package-standard.mdc` and `implementation-plans.mdc`. |
| `report` | `docs/report/<name>/` | Standalone review/audit reports |
| `review-testing` | `docs/review-testing/<name>/` | QA and testing artifacts |
| `communication` | `docs/communication/<name>/` | Communication and context docs |
| `analysis` | `docs/analysis/<name>/` | Feature/branch analysis (see below) |

## Analysis Category Structure

The `analysis` category is used by the `feature-analyzer` skill and any branch/feature analysis tasks.

```
docs/analysis/<feature-name>/
  report.md
  implementation-plan.md
```

- `report.md` — detailed analysis of changes, ticket, cross-repo findings
- `implementation-plan.md` — actionable implementation plan derived from the analysis
- Add `ru`/`en`/`ai` variants only if the user explicitly asks for them; the
  default is the single `en` files shown above.

## Naming Rules
- Ask user for `<name>` first.
- Use semantic, kebab-case folder names.
- Keep filenames deterministic: `<name>.md` unless user asks another convention.

## Output Contract
- Every generated document MUST be Markdown (`.md`).
- Structure must be explicit with headings and actionable sections.
- Code examples must be fenced code blocks.

## Relationship to `jobs/`

`docs/` and `jobs/` are **separate systems**:
- `docs/` — general project documentation (requirements, plans, reports, analysis). Managed by this rule.
- `jobs/` — orchestrator pipeline artifacts. Each job folder documents one orchestrated task end-to-end.

Standalone skill invocations continue to use `docs/analysis/`. Only orchestrator-driven work produces output in `jobs/`.
See `core/jobs-documentation.mdc` for the `jobs/` system.

## Prohibited
- Date-stamped folders anywhere under `<DOCS_ROOT>`.
- Language variants the user did not ask for.
- Partial updates to language variants that do exist.
- Writing docs outside the requested category path without confirmation.
- Mixing `report`/`implementation-plan` content in the same file.
